# Codex Pasted Text Attachment Repair

## Goal

Keep long pasted text usable in Codex Desktop. Prefer the native repair first; if the current Codex build still rejects long text, use the automatic Codex-only fallback that converts long clipboard text into a `.txt` file attachment.

## Fast Path

1. Check native attachment storage:

```powershell
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "$env:USERPROFILE\.codex\skills\codex-pasted-text-attachment-repair\scripts\repair-pasted-text-attachments.ps1"
```

2. Repair missing local state if needed:

```powershell
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "$env:USERPROFILE\.codex\skills\codex-pasted-text-attachment-repair\scripts\repair-pasted-text-attachments.ps1" -Repair
```

3. If native long paste still fails, install and start the fallback:

```powershell
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "$env:USERPROFILE\.codex\skills\codex-pasted-text-attachment-repair\scripts\install-auto-longtext-fileclip.ps1" -Start
```

4. Verify with a controlled long text:

```powershell
Add-Type -AssemblyName System.Windows.Forms
$sample = ('CODEX_LONG_TEXT_ATTACHMENT_TEST_0123456789 ' * 150)
[System.Windows.Forms.Clipboard]::SetText($sample)
Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 800
(New-Object -ComObject WScript.Shell).AppActivate('Codex') | Out-Null
Start-Sleep -Seconds 3
[System.Windows.Forms.Clipboard]::ContainsFileDropList()
```

Success means the result is `True`, the log has fresh `PENDING` and `ACTIVATED` lines, and the file path is under:

```text
%USERPROFILE%\.codex\manual-paste-attachments
```

## What To Check

- Native attachment root: `%USERPROFILE%\.codex\attachments`
- Fallback log: `%USERPROFILE%\.codex\manual-paste-attachments\auto-longtext-fileclip.log`
- Fallback process: match `\auto-longtext-fileclip.ps1`
- Watchdog task: `CodexAutoLongTextWatchdog`
- Startup shortcut: `%APPDATA%\Microsoft\Windows\Start Menu\Programs\Startup\Codex Auto LongText ON.lnk`

Use a strict process match. Do not match plain `auto-longtext-fileclip.ps1`, because `watch-auto-longtext-fileclip.ps1` contains the same suffix and can create a false positive.

```powershell
$needle='\auto-longtext-fileclip.ps1'
Get-CimInstance Win32_Process |
  Where-Object { $_.Name -match '^powershell(\.exe)?$' -and $_.CommandLine -like ('*' + $needle + '*') } |
  Select-Object ProcessId,CreationDate,CommandLine
```

## Fallback Behavior

- Ignores short text below `MinChars` so normal paste still works.
- Saves long text as `codex-pasted-text-<timestamp>-<hash>.txt`.
- Changes the clipboard into a file-drop attachment only when Codex is foreground.
- Retries clipboard reads/writes because Windows clipboard can be briefly locked.
- Keeps the generated file on the clipboard for a few seconds after Codex becomes foreground.
- Does not cancel a prepared attachment merely because another app briefly changes the clipboard; it expires after a timeout.
- Installs `CodexAutoLongTextWatchdog`, which checks once per minute and restarts the converter if it has exited.

## Cursor/Kilo Long Text Mode

Observed on 2026-06-30: short paste worked in Kilo/Cursor, but long paste did not become a file-style message. The existing converter was healthy for Codex Desktop, but its foreground check only activated for Codex windows. Kilo/Cursor needs an explicit target mode.

Use this only when the user wants long text pasted into Kilo/Claude Code/Cursor agent panels to become a `.txt` file-drop clipboard:

```powershell
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "$env:USERPROFILE\.codex\skills\codex-pasted-text-attachment-repair\scripts\install-auto-longtext-fileclip.ps1" -Start -TargetMode "Codex,CursorKilo"
```

Default mode remains `Codex` to avoid surprising normal Cursor editor paste. In `CursorKilo` mode, short text below `MinChars` is ignored, and long text activates when the foreground process is Cursor.

## Common Fixes

- No fresh log lines after a failed paste: start or reinstall the fallback with `install-auto-longtext-fileclip.ps1 -Start`.
- Process missing after previously working: confirm the watchdog task exists, then reinstall/start.
- Log shows clipboard busy errors: restart fallback; the current scripts retry clipboard operations.
- Repeated same long text is skipped or cancelled: ensure the deployed script is the latest copy from this skill.
- Codex still shows the original toast while fallback is running: wait a moment after switching to Codex, then paste again; confirm clipboard contains a file-drop list.

## Scripts

- `repair-pasted-text-attachments.ps1`: check and repair native `%USERPROFILE%\.codex\attachments`.
- `fix-codex-longtext-attachment.ps1`: command-pack style diagnosis; patches only safe writable non-WindowsApps `app.asar`; otherwise reports fallback.
- `install-auto-longtext-fileclip.ps1`: copy scripts to runtime folder, create shortcuts, register watchdog, optionally start/stop.
- `auto-longtext-fileclip.ps1`: background converter.
- `watch-auto-longtext-fileclip.ps1`: scheduled watchdog that restarts the converter if missing.
- `clipboard-to-txt.ps1`: manual emergency fallback that writes clipboard text to a `.txt` file.
- `START/STOP/STATUS_Auto_LongText_FileClip.cmd`: desktop shortcuts for non-technical use.

`-Stop` must disable the watchdog and remove the Startup shortcut; otherwise the watchdog will restart the converter after the user turns it off. `-Start` reinstalls the runtime scripts, Startup shortcut, watchdog task, and converter process.

## Safety

Do not modify `C:\Program Files\WindowsApps` or an MSIX package in place. If only a Windows Store/MSIX Codex install exists, use the fallback rather than patching the app package.

